+- X/Twitter: third-party current topic ranking, with unknown volumes labeled as unavailable.
+- TikTok: official public preview of three hashtags by supported country, with reported post/view metrics and seven-day period. Global maps to US.
+- YouTube without a key: official weekly top music-video charts, not all-category realtime trending videos. US, Japan and UK were tested. Chart dates and weekly view counts are preserved. The optional YouTube Data API path is also retained; no real key was used to validate it.
+- Instagram: logged-out public Reels recommendation sample, rendered with ordinary Chromium. No login or paid API is required. Missing view counts are not invented. Only global sample mode is supported.
+- Douyin: official public mainland-China hot lists, with heat scores and source timestamps. Global and cn select China. Heat is not views.
 
-Ask Claude *"What's trending on TikTok right now?"* and get real answers.
+Public web interfaces may change or deny access. Failures are reported explicitly; the server does not bypass logins/challenges or substitute static tags as verified trends. Broader coverage and multi-worker operation are outside the verified local scope.
 
