+Startup creates or upgrades the database schema and schedules an initial scrape plus six-hour refreshes. Existing region/configuration data is preserved by the upgrade. The workspace root also supplies `setup.sh` and `manage-service.sh` for persistent local database storage and supervised operation.
 
-## 🌐 REST API
+MCP SDK is constrained to 1.x for API compatibility. The installed `social-trends-mcp` console entry point correctly starts the async server. Browser sources require Playwright's Chromium installation as well as the Python package.
 
-For production use, deploy the full API service with PostgreSQL and auto-refresh.
+## MCP tools
 
-| Method | Path | Description |
-|--------|------|-------------|
-| GET | `/api/v1/trends` | All platforms latest data |
-| GET | `/api/v1/trends/{platform}` | Single platform trends |
-| GET | `/api/v1/trends/history/{platform}` | Historical trends |
-| POST | `/api/v1/refresh` | Manual refresh trigger |
-| GET | `/api/v1/health` | Service health + stats |
-| GET | `/docs` | Interactive Swagger UI |
-| WS | `/ws/trends` | WebSocket real-time push |
