-## 🐳 Docker Deployment
-
-Full production stack in one command:
-
-```bash
-git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/social-trends-mcp.git
-cd social-trends-mcp
-cp .env.example .env
-# Edit .env — at minimum set YOUTUBE_API_KEY
-
-docker-compose up -d
-```
+`get_trends`, `get_all_trends`, `exact_search`, `search_trends` (exact-search alias), `discover_search`, and `list_regions`.
 
-This starts PostgreSQL + App (4 workers) + Nginx.
+Search matches observed current feeds, not every post on the underlying platform. Discovery uses local keyword expansion by default; optional configured LLM expansion is separate and can be metered. Partial source coverage is exposed.
 
----
+## REST
 
-## ⚙️ Configuration
+- GET `/api/v1/trends?region=global&limit=30`
+- GET `/api/v1/trends/twitter?region=jp`
+- GET `/api/v1/trends/history/twitter?region=jp&hours=72`
+- GET `/api/v1/search/exact?q=robotics&platforms=twitter,tiktok`
+- GET `/api/v1/search/discover?q=AI`
+- POST `/api/v1/refresh?platform=twitter&region=jp` (202 accepted)
+- GET `/api/v1/health`, `/api/v1/platforms`, `/api/v1/regions`
+- WS `/ws/trends` (ping/pong and committed `trends_updated` events)
+- GET `/docs`
 
-| Variable | Required | Description |
-|----------|----------|-------------|
-| `YOUTUBE_API_KEY` | Recommended | [Get free](https://console.cloud.google.com/apis) — 10K units/day |
-| `TWITTER_BEARER_TOKEN` | Optional | [$200/mo](https://developer.x.com/) — fallback works without it |
-| `INSTAGRAM_ACCESS_TOKEN` | Optional | [Meta Developer](https://developers.facebook.com/) — fallback works without it |
-| `TIKTOK_PROXY` | Optional | Proxy URL if TikTok blocks your IP |
-| `SCRAPE_INTERVAL_HOURS` | Optional | Auto-refresh interval (default: 6) |
+Snapshots retain their requested region and topics retain their actual source region. Region queries never substitute another country's snapshot. Missing or unsupported data is explicit. Freshness describes retrieval age; source chart/post periods remain separate. Health degrades when a configured feed fails, is missing or becomes stale.
 
-**Zero-config is possible** — every platform has fallback scrapers that work without API keys.
+## Optional configuration
 
----
+`.env.example` lists available settings. `INSTAGRAM_SOURCE=browser` is the default. A SocialCrawl key alone does not activate paid requests: `INSTAGRAM_SOURCE=socialcrawl` must be explicitly selected. There is no automatic paid fallback. Hashtag suggestions are a separate opt-in mode.
 
-## 🤝 Contributing
+`SCRAPE_INTERVAL_HOURS` accepts 1–168. Unknown Compose-only environment-file variables are ignored. Source chains are bounded and duplicate concurrent refreshes for the same platform/region are skipped.
 
-We welcome contributions! See [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md).
+The Dockerfile includes Chromium and its runtime libraries, uses a non-root app user and one worker, and excludes local `.env` files from the image. The image was exercised against a fresh database with all five sources healthy. Full Nginx/public HTTPS deployment and shared multi-replica scheduling/event delivery were not verified.
 
-**Easy wins:** Add a new platform (Threads, Bluesky...), improve scraper quality, add MCP tools, translations.
